# Bundled assets are embedded into the binary at compile time and verified
# against the committed SHA-256 manifest (assets/manifest.txt). Any checkout-
# time conversion — especially LF -> CRLF on Windows — changes the bytes and
# breaks verification. Mark everything under assets/ as binary (-text), and
# the native-library / traineddata extensions explicitly so real binaries
# dropped in later are also immune even if they live outside assets/.
assets/** -text
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.dll binary
*.traineddata binary

# Test fixture PDFs are parsed by lopdf and byte-compared in tests. Small
# hand-built fixtures contain no early NUL bytes, so git's binary
# auto-detection can miss them and CRLF-convert them on Windows checkout,
# corrupting xref offsets. Keep every fixture byte-identical everywhere.
tests/fixtures/** -text
*.pdf binary
